n to her back. Pain is severe in intensity, and refractory to simple analgesics. Ultrasound and contrast enhanced CT scan (CECT) confirmed the diagnosis and showed a dilated pancreatic duct. Which of the following is the likely recommended surgical procedure of choice? (LQ)&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Vagotomy with Antrectomy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Vagotomy with Gastrojejunostomy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Whipple&#x27;s Procedure&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Longitudinal Pancreaticojejunostomy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;D. Longitudinal Pancreaticojejunostomy&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/surgery55.jpg&quot;], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correct Answer (D)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/dqb_vod/11812651704714493/11812651704714493.m3u8&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;Pain relief in chronic pancreatitis can be obtained by destruction of: (AIIMS May 2014)&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Celiac ganglia&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Vagus nerve&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Anterolateral column of spinal cord&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;None of the above&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;A. Celiac ganglia&quot;, &q