ect&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Calcium channel blockers&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Peripheral artery bypass&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Pentoxifylline&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;A. Smoking cessation&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/course_file_meta/141680221.jpg&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A 55-year-old man had the painless lesions shown here. Biopsy reveals carcinoma in situ. What is this condition?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Primary syphilis&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Erythroplasia of Queyrat&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Plasma cell balanitis of Zoon&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Circinate balanitis of Reiter’s syndrome&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;B. Erythroplasia of Queyrat&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/course_file_meta/647576422.jpg&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A 40 year old male patient presented with mild abdominal pain, mild constipation with a feeling of incomplete evacuation and mucus in stools for the past 4 years. On examination, tenderness present on left iliac fossa. Barium enema picture is given below. The most likely diagnosis is:&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Ulcerative colitis&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Diverticular disease of colon&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Irritable bowel syndrome&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Carcinoma colon&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;B. Diverticular disease of colon&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/course_file_meta/466255123.jpg&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A 65-year-old woman presents with fatigue, right flank pain, and ankle edema. Laboratory studies show increased liver enzyme values and microscopic hematuria. The picture CT scan abdomen is given below. What is the diagnosis?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Choledocholithiasis&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Nephrolithiasis&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Hepatocellular carcinoma&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Renal cell carcinoma&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;D. Renal cell carcinoma&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/course_file_meta/523272324.jpg&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quo