robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;What is the size of the cannula shown in the below image?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;16 G&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;18 G&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;20 G&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;22 G&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;C. 20 G&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/14(227).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A 45-year-old man is diagnosed with an indirect inguinal hernia. The surgeon uses the suture material given in the image below for the hernia repair. It is a polyamide polymer that undergoes degradation and loses tensile strength at the rate of 15-20% every year. Identify the suture material.&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Polyester&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Polypropylene&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Nylon&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Polyglycaprone&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;C. Nylon&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/15(238).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A young man with a history of blunt abdominal trauma was brought to the emergency department. He was hemodynamically unstable, and a FAST examination revealed free fluid. An immediate laparotomy was done. The maneuver shown in the image below was performed due to severe bleeding near the liver. However, the bleeding continued. What could be the probable source of the bleeding in this case? FAST-Focussed assessment with sonography in trauma&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Hepatic arterial bleeding&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Hepatic vein bleeding&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Portal venous bleeding&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Both hepatic arterial and Portal venous bleeding&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;B. Hepatic vein bleeding&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/16(213).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A chronic alcoholic presents to the emergency room with bloody vomitus. Vital signs show a BP of 90/70 mm Hg, pulse 110 bpm, and SpO2-97%. Physical examination shows scleral icterus and a distended abdomen with spider nevi. The bleeding is immediately controlled using the instrument shown in the image. Identify the instrument?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Minnesota tube&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Sengstaken Blakemore tube&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Linton Nachlas tube&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Ewald’s tube&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;B. Sengstaken Blakemore tube&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/18(173).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;Which of the following is the principle behind the wound-healing procedure shown in the image below?.&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Negative pressure wound therapy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Positive pressure wound therapy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Foam therapy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Sponge therapy&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;A. Negative pressure wound therapy&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/19(164).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;The operating surgeon performed the following suture technique on the skin after appendicectomy surgery. This is called&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Mattress suture&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Subcuticular suture&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Continuous suture&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Interrupted suture&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;A. Mattress suture&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/20(171).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;The procedure shown in the image below is being performed on a 35-year-old male patient, who presented with complaints of dysphagia, regurgitation, and chest pain. His barium swallow showed a bird’s beak appearance near the gastroesophageal junction. What is the procedure performed on this patient known as?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;NOTES&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;B&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;SILS&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;C&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;POEM&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: true}, {&quot;label&quot;: &quot;D&quot;, &quot;text&quot;: &quot;ROSE&quot;, &quot;correct&quot;: false}], &quot;correct_answer&quot;: &quot;C. POEM&quot;, &quot;question_images&quot;: [&quot;https://d2enu63wt1sf3u.cloudfront.net/ckfinder/files/1(855).png&quot;], &quot;explanation_images&quot;: [], &quot;explanation&quot;: &quot;&lt;p&gt;@dams_new_robot&lt;/p&gt;&quot;, &quot;bot&quot;: &quot;@dams_new_robot&quot;, &quot;video&quot;: &quot;&quot;}, {&quot;text&quot;: &quot;A 55-year-old male presented with verrucous carcinoma around the glans of the penis. Examination reveals that the inguinal lymph nodes are not enlarged. What is the appropriate management for this patient?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [{&quot;label&quot;: &quot;A&quot;, &quot;text&quo